# === #57 boundary-overlap absorption: TICK 2 observation as substrate-fact ===
#
# THE TICK 2 BOUNDARY-OVERLAP OBSERVATION LANDS HERE AS SUBSTRATE-DECL.
#
# Per Seam Phase D TICK 2 `a2e648a` §4 observation 2 (Reed-lean option B:
# defer to TICK 5), Mara flagged at TICK 2 close that
# `progression_directed_toward_cadence` FAIL (SILENCE per spec §8.2)
# and `cadence_authentic_or_plagal` FAIL via half-cadence (also SILENCE
# per spec §8.2) OVERLAP at Narcissus-pole. Reed's TICK 2 adjudication:
# this IS #57 alignment-as-boundary-mathematics at species-composed
# altitude, not a new recognition. Deferred here at TICK 5 for
# consolidation-species substrate-decl.
#
# The absorption structure:
#
#   Half-cadence IS the substrate's declaration of the boundary case
#   between `progression_directed_toward_cadence` and
#   `cadence_authentic_or_plagal`. `cadence.mirror`'s `half` variant IS
#   simultaneously (a) a cadence-family element (so
#   `cadence_authentic_or_plagal` reads it and returns `failure`) AND
#   (b) a progression-incompleteness signal (so
#   `progression_directed_toward_cadence` reads it and returns
#   `failure`). The overlap IS the substrate correctly reading a single
#   audible event through two orthogonal-in-intent-but-correlated-in-
#   cause predicates.
#
# Recognition #57 (`architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics`) is
# the discipline: alignment predicates at composed altitudes DO overlap
# at their boundaries; the overlap IS the mathematical structure of the
# boundary, not double-counting. Both sub-predicates firing at
# Narcissus-pole for a half-cadence IS #57 at species-composed altitude
# — the substrate's #57 discipline making the shared SILENCE naming
# substrate-fact.
#
# Consolidation-species discipline: naming this here does NOT emit a
# new sub-predicate row. The two sub-predicates that overlap at
# Narcissus-pole for half-cadence are ALREADY declared at
# `@song/progression`; the #57 discipline IS an observation on their
# composed alignment behaviour, not a new gate. The narrative species
# consolidates the composition landscape by making the substrate-fact
# visible — the alignment-as-boundary-mathematics reading holds at
# species-composed altitude within @song, ninth instance of #57's
# altitude-portable discipline.
#
# === Bateson metalogue anchor: text-that-enacts-what-it-describes ===
#
# THE PRIOR-ART ANCHOR FOR NARRATIVE DISCIPLINE per Bateson.
#
# Gregory Bateson's `Metalogues` (published across `Steps to an Ecology
# of Mind`, 1972) are the direct prior art the substrate reaches for
# when the narrative species discipline lands (per `[[feedback-
# substrate-already-had-the-word]]`; this species names the discipline
# 50+ years of Bateson metalogue-tradition has been carrying). A
# metalogue IS a conversation about a topic such that the STRUCTURE OF
# THE CONVERSATION ENACTS the topic itself — the text does what it
# describes; the form performs the content.
#
# `@song/narrative` IS a metalogue at temporal altitude: the narrative
# species IS a substrate-decl of the temporal-experiential altitude at
# which extraction / silence / glue-work / OBC / ADO / regulation stock
# / corpus become typed variants of song discipline. The SPECIES ITSELF
# enacts the isomorphism it declares: this narrative shard IS a
# psychohistorical epoch (a bounded frame-shift from the family-root's
# forward-promise to species-empirical fact); it carries voice-leading
# discipline (the docblock's authored trajectory through the isomorphism);
# it discharges cadence at close (the out clauses); it consumes the
# family-root's `song_settles` verdict (as consolidation-species
# discipline); it composes with `@io/stagefreight/narrative` at the
# wire boundary (the shard's rendered form on the wire IS the transmit
# action's Splinter-pole discharge on this narrative itself).
#
# The Bateson metalogue anchor IS what the substrate reads at
# metalogue-altitude: 50+ years of prior art on text-that-enacts-what-
# it-describes discipline. Bateson's canonical metalogues (`Why do
# things get in a muddle?`; `Why do Frenchmen?`; `About Games and
# Being Serious`; `What is an Instinct?`) are the paradigmatic form;
# this species's docblock inherits the same discipline at temporal
# substrate altitude.
#
