# === Turchin cliodynamics: optional prior-art anchor ===
#
# The psychohistorical vocabulary the substrate lifts here has an
# adjacent prior-art tradition in Peter Turchin's cliodynamics (`Ages
# of Discord`, 2016; `Secular Cycles` with Sergey Nefedov, 2009):
# quantitative-historical dynamics as the structural discipline of
# multi-epoch trajectory analysis. Cliodynamics reads history as a
# multi-epoch trajectory where each epoch's regulation-stock replenish-
# ment or depletion structures the transition to the next epoch;
# elite-overproduction / immiseration / instability metrics are the
# quantitative form of what Alex's corpus names in qualitative
# psychohistorical vocabulary. This is complementary anchor territory;
# not load-bearing to the isomorphism, but useful prior art for the
# corpus-as-composed-cohomology reading at multi-epoch altitude.
#
# === #S3 LANDED consolidation: five-op temporal specialisation ===
#
# THE CONSOLIDATION WITNESS OF RECOGNITION #S3 AT THE POST-PROMOTION
# ALTITUDE.
#
# Recognition #S3 (five-operation temporal specialisation) PROMOTED
# CANDIDATE → LANDED at Seam Phase D `10c34cf` after TICK 3
# (`docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-phase-d-arc-6-tick-3-song-voice-and-
# s3-promotion.md`). Per family-root `shards/song.mirror` §"Recognition
# candidates surfaced" #S3, at temporal altitude `@song` specialises
# the five operations of the prism trait. Narrative's role in the
# LANDED consolidation is CONFIRMATION at the psychohistorical +
# wire-projection altitude, not extension: it demonstrates that the
# five-op temporal specialisation survives a fourth species-altitude
# witness without new sub-predicate emission. The five operations
# discharge at this species by INHERITANCE from the family-root prism
# block plus specialisation through the narrative-as-sheaf-section
# discipline:
#
#   focus @ narrative   = attend to ONE narrative arc at a time; the
#                         psychohistorical epoch's authored line
#                         filters the corpus to a single section.
#   project @ narrative = down-project the multi-narrative corpus to
#                         a single narrative's structural profile
#                         (the sheaf's stalk at one local frame).
#   split @ narrative   = decompose the corpus into constituent
#                         narratives (multi-section sheaf preparation
#                         at organisational altitude).
#   shift @ narrative   = advance the narrative arc from one epoch's
#                         closure to the next epoch's opening
#                         (inter-narrative transition; the corpus's
#                         epoch-boundary).
#   settle @ narrative  = discharge the narrative's `transmit` event;
#                         the wire-projection ships the settled
#                         section through `@io/stagefreight/narrative`
#                         at the @io altitude; the psychohistorical
#                         epoch's sheaf-section enters the corpus.
#
# The five operations discharge cleanly at narrative altitude; #S3
# LANDED consolidates through this species (SECOND consolidation-species
# witness after movement TICK 4 `4efbf16`) without requiring new sub-
# predicate emission. Two consolidation-species witnesses (movement +
# narrative) confirm the LANDED status at post-promotion altitude.
