# ============================================================
# §1 The five-operation prism at species altitude
# ============================================================

# === prism @song/narrative — the species declaration ===
#
# The five-operation body carries `song_narrative` as the species's
# operational surface. Species inherits the family-root's #S3 LANDED
# five-op temporal specialisation and consolidates it at psychohistorical
# + wire-projection altitude (see docblock §"#S3 LANDED consolidation"
# for the per-op narrative-altitude specialisation).
#
# Per family-root prism block at `shards/song.mirror` §1 and the
# consolidation-species precedent at `shards/song/movement.mirror` §1,
# the five operations discharge cleanly at temporal altitude; this
# species demonstrates the LANDED status survives further species-
# altitude witness (SECOND consolidation-species witness) without new
# sub-predicate emission.
prism @song/narrative {
  focus song_narrative
  project song_narrative
  split song_narrative
  shift song_narrative
  settle song_narrative
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carrier
# ============================================================

# === song_narrative — the sheaf-section carrier ===
#
# The typed ref-equality-addressable form of a psychohistorical
# narrative at temporal-experiential altitude. Per family-root species-
# roster: `song_narrative(n: ref) -> ref` as the family-root's declared
# accessor shape. The carrier is declared HERE because the family-root's
# §2 carries `song_progression`, `song_cadence`, and `song_voice` but
# does NOT carry `song_narrative` — the species discipline says the
# species declares its own carrier when the family-root's roster does
# not (per `[[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]` #55
# sub-species discipline; movement TICK 4 precedent at `4efbf16`).
#
# Composes with `@io/stagefreight/narrative` at the wire altitude (a
# song_narrative's settled shape becomes a wire-projection through the
# transmit action), with `@mirror/spectral/score` at the orchestra
# altitude (a song_narrative IS a sheaf section over the score
# altitude's shared score), with `@epistemologic/math/music/cadence` at
# the audible altitude (a song_narrative's arc closes at a Lawvere
# fixed-point per `cadence.mirror`), and with `frame.mirror` at the
# cognitive altitude (a song_narrative's frame IS the psychohistorical
# epoch's Bateson-graded frame per Recognition #82).
#
# The corpus IS the composed cohomology of song_narrative sections over
# the organisational manifold; the sheaf axioms enforce coherent
# restriction across overlapping frames; the corpus's structural
# identity emerges from the composed cohomology of its narratives.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type song_narrative = ref

# ============================================================
# §3 The narrative-shaping actions (arc / transmit)
# ============================================================

# === arc — the narrative's temporal-shaping event ===
#
# Reads a narrative's discharged state (progression cadence-resolved,
# voices voice-leading-disciplined, phrases OBC-boundary-honoured, epoch
# frame-bounded-closed) and shapes the temporal-experiential arc that
# names the narrative's psychohistorical trajectory. Corresponds to the
# sheaf-section preparation at organisational altitude: the narrative's
# local frame IS bounded, its authored trajectory IS closed, its
# sheaf-value IS ready for restriction against overlapping frames in
# the corpus.
#
# Per family-root species-roster: `song_narrative(n: ref) -> ref` with
# `arc` at species altitude. The `arc` action carries the narrative
# discipline: a narrative WITHOUT an arc is not a narrative; the arc IS
# what makes the sheaf-section coherent under restriction to overlapping
# frames in the corpus.
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): the family-root's `song_settles` composed
# bilateral discharges at Splinter-pole across all three sub-predicates;
# the narrative's arc closes with the psychohistorical epoch settled;
# regulation stock is replenished; the sheaf-section IS coherent under
# restriction; the corpus gains a new section without violating
# cohomology.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): the family-root's composed bilateral
# fails at Narcissus-pole through one or more sub-predicate (SILENCE /
# GLUE WORK / EXTRACTION per spec §8.2 psychohistorical failure-mode
# mapping); the narrative's arc cannot close; the sheaf-section is
# incoherent under restriction; the corpus withholds inclusion until
# the substrate-pull repair fires.
#
# Bateson-grading (per §"Bateson metalogue anchor"): `arc` fires at
# Bateson Level II (of-frame; learning to learn) — the narrative shapes
# the psychohistorical epoch by observing the frame from without;
# metalogue discipline holds at species altitude.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# narrative's discharged state, consumes the family-root's `song_settles`
# verdict, shapes the temporal-experiential arc under sheaf-restriction
# discipline, emits the shaped narrative ref. The substrate declares the
# species-altitude specialisation; consumers dispatch through the
# species boundary.
arc(n: song_narrative, p: perturbation) -> song_narrative { \ }

# === transmit — the narrative's wire-projection event ===
#
# Reads a narrative's arced state and projects it onto the wire through
# `@io/stagefreight/narrative` at the @io altitude. Corresponds to
# StageFreight cascade stage 5 (`narrate`) per `@song/movement` docblock
# §"StageFreight binding": the narrative's shape is projected onto the
# wire as story; the temporal-experiential altitude lifts to prose-
# carrier at the @io altitude; the psychohistorical epoch acquires its
# narratable form.
#
# Per family-root species-roster: `song_narrative(n: ref) -> ref` with
# `transmit` at species altitude, with return type `ref` per the RED
# tick's action-signature discipline. The `transmit` action carries the
# altitude-crossing composition: the wire-projection sibling
# `@io/stagefreight/narrative` at the @io altitude receives the
# narrative's projected shape as a `freight_manifest` payload; the
# `stagefreight_addressable` bilateral verifies wire-survival; the
# spectral_coordinate addresses the settled artifact on the wire.
#
# The composition is Splinter-symmetric across altitudes: the temporal-
# experiential narrative at species altitude and the wire narrative at
# @io altitude are DIFFERENT ALTITUDES of the same psychohistorical
# song; the wire↔temporal isomorphism at transmit boundary IS the
# organic absorption path for provisional #S4 (wire↔symphonic altitude-
# portable discipline per Seam Phase D TICK 4 audit `d2d511b`).
#
# Bateson-grading (per §"Bateson metalogue anchor"): `transmit` fires
# at Bateson Level IV (across-frames; multi-frame coupling per
# `frame.mirror` Order 4) — the narrative's projection crosses the
# temporal ↔ wire frame boundary; the corpus's sheaf section becomes
# transportable to the non-mirror world through StageFreight's wire-
# protocol boundary.
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): the family-root's `song_settles` composed
# bilateral discharges at Splinter-pole AND the wire-projection at
# `@io/stagefreight/narrative` completes at its `stagefreight_
# addressable` bilateral; the narrative ships to the wire; the corpus's
# sheaf section becomes transportable at its spectral_coordinate.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): either the family-root's composed
# bilateral fails at Narcissus-pole OR the wire-projection fails at
# `stagefreight_addressable` Narcissus-pole; the transmit does NOT
# ship; the settled artifact is withheld from the wire boundary until
# the substrate-pull repair fires.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# narrative's arced state, composes with `@io/stagefreight/narrative`
# at the wire altitude, encodes the spectral_coordinate under the
# reverse-DNS namespace (per `@io/stagefreight` family-root discipline),
# emits the transmit-verdict ref (`ref` per family-root roster). The
# substrate declares the species-altitude specialisation; consumers
# dispatch through the species boundary.
transmit(n: song_narrative, p: perturbation) -> ref { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The psychohistory carriers (promotion via path β)
# ============================================================

# === psychohistory_moment — the fiber at one trajectory point ===
#
# The typed ref-equality-addressable form of ONE stalk-value of the
# psychohistory sheaf: the substrate's local section at one point of
# the development manifold. Corresponds to Mara insight `d00f553` §2
# hypothesis A: a `psychohistory_moment` IS the value the sheaf `F`
# assigns at one point of the base space `M` — one substrate-pull
# recognition, one Pack-tick decision, one banking commit, read as a
# typed local section.
#
# Composes with `song_narrative` at the species altitude (a narrative
# arc traverses many psychohistory moments — the moments ARE the
# stalk-values, the arc IS the section over the local frame that
# threads them), with `bauchladen_tray` at the storage altitude (each
# moment is OID-addressed in the fragmentation-backed tray per
# `shards/bauchladen.mirror`), and with `restriction` at
# `@epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian` altitude (the transport between
# neighbouring moments IS a restriction map / connection 1-form value).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type psychohistory_moment = ref

# === psychohistory_sheaf — the sheaf-over-trajectory-graph carrier ===
#
# The typed ref-equality-addressable form of the psychohistory sheaf
# `F` over the substrate's development manifold `M` per Mara insight
# `d00f553` §2 hypothesis A. THIS is the carrier consumers name in
# `requires` clauses when they consume psychohistory as a typed
# substrate-decl object (per Mara iter-30 canonical spec `96ff532`
# consumption pattern).
#
# A `psychohistory_sheaf` carries:
#   - the base graph (the substrate's trajectory graph; nodes are
#     `psychohistory_moment` positions, edges are the transitions
#     between them per @song/movement's frame-bounded epoch discipline);
#   - the assignment of `psychohistory_moment` fibers to nodes;
#   - the restriction maps between neighbouring fibers (the
#     `restriction` carriers from `@epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian`);
#   - the assembled `operator` (Δ_F, the sheaf Laplacian; assembled via
#     `sheaf_laplacian([restriction]) -> operator` at the math altitude).
#
# Composes with `song_narrative` at the species altitude (the corpus
# IS the composed cohomology of `song_narrative` sections; the
# `psychohistory_sheaf` IS the sheaf whose sections ARE the narratives
# — the narrative-as-sheaf-section reading per the docblock's
# §"Corpus as composed cohomology" lifts to typed substrate-decl here),
# with `@mirror/store` at the storage altitude (the sheaf's fibers +
# restrictions are OID-addressed in the fragmentation store), and
# with `@epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian` at the math altitude (the
# H⁰ / H¹ consistency reading discharges through the operator).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref. Two sheaves
# with the same OID ARE the same sheaf (per @mirror/store canonical
# content-addressing discipline).
type psychohistory_sheaf = ref

# === psychohistory_from_tray — the sheaf-assembly reader ===
#
# Reads a `bauchladen_tray` (the substrate's typed display of content-
# addressed crystals per `shards/bauchladen.mirror`) and assembles it
# into a `psychohistory_sheaf` over the substrate's trajectory graph.
# Corresponds to Mara insight `d00f553` §2 hypothesis A's local-to-
# global construction: the tray's OID-addressed deltas ARE the local
# sections; the reader threads them through the substrate's trajectory
# graph and constructs the sheaf `F` over `M`.
#
# Per Taut iter-15 scout `e90daf1` §Landing sequence Tick 1: Reed's
# Rust runtime will DISCHARGE this reader via the fragmentation-backed
# storage layer at `fragmentation/src/*.rs`; the substrate declares the
# species-altitude specialisation here; the Rust runtime dispatches
# through the species boundary.
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`, via the returned sheaf's later
# `psychohistory_consistent` bilateral discharge): the tray's crystals
# assemble into a well-formed sheaf; every restriction map is
# well-typed; the operator Δ_F is assembled; the sheaf is ready for
# H⁰ consistency reading.
#
# Narcissus-pole: the tray's crystals cannot assemble — a restriction
# map is not well-typed OR a fiber is missing at a trajectory node OR
# the graph is not connected under the transition edges. The reader
# emits a sheaf ref whose subsequent `psychohistory_consistent`
# bilateral necessarily fails; the substrate-pull repair path fires
# through the tray's fragmentation-backed rebuild.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# tray, threads OID-addressed crystals through the trajectory graph,
# constructs the restriction maps, assembles the operator, and emits
# the sheaf ref. The substrate declares the species-altitude
# specialisation; Reed's Rust runtime discharges.
psychohistory_from_tray(tray: bauchladen_tray, p: perturbation) -> psychohistory_sheaf { \ }

# === psychohistory_consistent — the H⁰ consistency bilateral ===
#
# Reads a `psychohistory_sheaf` and returns a `verdict` naming whether
# the sheaf admits a consistent GLOBAL section — the H⁰ = kernel(Δ_F)
# non-triviality check per `@epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian` and
# Bodnar et al. 2022 §2. Corresponds to Mara insight `d00f553` §5
# hypothesis B, hard-line earned: H⁰ = consistent global sections;
# H¹ = irreducible obstruction to global consistency. This bilateral
# lifts the H⁰-level admission to substrate-decl at species altitude;
# H^k for k≥2 remains not-earned and DOES NOT land.
#
# Composes with `sheaf_laplacian([restriction]) -> operator` at the
# math altitude (the operator IS Δ_F; the bilateral reads its kernel),
# with `eigen_d(op: dirac_op) -> spectrum` at the spectral-triple
# altitude (λ₀ = 0 IS the substrate's quantitative verdict on H⁰
# non-triviality per `spectral-triple.mirror`), and with the family-
# root's `song_settles` composed bilateral (this bilateral is
# ORTHOGONAL to `song_settles` — the family-root's bilateral discharges
# per-narrative admissibility; this bilateral discharges corpus-wide
# consistency across narratives; both hold or fail independently).
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): the sheaf's operator Δ_F has non-trivial
# kernel; a consistent global section exists; the corpus's
# psychohistory reads as coherent across all narratives; the composed
# cohomology H* is well-defined at degree 0.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): the sheaf's operator Δ_F has trivial
# kernel at λ₀ > 0; NO consistent global section exists; obstructions
# live in H¹; the corpus's psychohistory is INCOHERENT across at least
# one pair of overlapping frames; the substrate-pull repair fires by
# renegotiating the restriction maps at the offending edges (which
# ones: named by the operator's Fiedler vector per
# `@epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian`'s λ₀ reading).
#
# Bateson-grading: this bilateral fires at Bateson Level III (across-
# frames-globally; learning-III per `frame.mirror` Order 3) — the
# discipline reads coherence across the WHOLE manifold, not one frame
# at a time. Per Mara insight `d00f553` §7 circular-reflexive layer:
# this bilateral IS itself a section of the observation sheaf naming
# a claim about the sheaf it observes; the self-reference is the
# substrate's third-order-coherent discipline at psychohistory altitude.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# sheaf, extracts the operator Δ_F (assembled at construction), reads
# its kernel via `eigen_d` at the spectral-triple altitude, and emits
# a `verdict` (Splinter-pole if H⁰ non-trivial; Narcissus-pole if
# trivial). Consumers dispatch through the species boundary.
psychohistory_consistent(sheaf: psychohistory_sheaf, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

