# altitude statement of trauma's stuck projection. Mara iter-34 §6-S4
# surfaced this as recursive surprise: same math at both altitudes,
# same Bayesian-brain-with-broken-precision-weighting reading. This
# tick lands the shape so the compiler altitude and the recognition
# altitude share the SAME `shadow_regime` classifier.

# === shadow — one projected shadow (candidate section under M) ===
#
# ONE shadow cast by one hypothetical direction (one candidate fate
# Model M's prism-op applied hypothetically) over the psychohistory
# sheaf. Per Reed's essay: the shadow's shape is overdetermined by
# its casting object; observer-in-Flatland reads the shadow; caster-
# in-Spaceland is the sheaf's global data.
#
# Composition per Mara iter-34 §4: Level 2 Gauge (direction IS the
# gauge choice) × Level 3 Transport (shadow IS transported section-
# value with holonomy residual) iterating through Level 4 Closure
# (Fate's autopoietic verdict; fixed-point IS settled coefficient
# mass on target eigenspace).
#
# Composes with `song_narrative` (narrative's arc threads shadows),
# `psychohistory_sheaf` (`shadow_ancestry` annotates), `Narcissus-
# pole coefficient` at mcp-spec-song-collapse §5.4/§6.3 (shadow's
# Narcissus-pole = mass on non-target eigenspaces), `@epistemologic/
# math/sheaf_laplacian` (Rayleigh λ₀ names the classifier's spectral
# witness).
#
# Prior art: Ghrist arXiv:2602.09313 (H⁰→Hⁿ hierarchy) + arXiv:2507.01226
# (torsor + sheaf-cohomology, July 2025); Penrose 1992 predates
# substrate 34y (Recognition #43-analogue per Mara iter-34 §6-S1).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type shadow = ref

# === shadow_regime — the three-regime classifier ===
#
# Typed enumeration of the cohomological regimes per Mara iter-34
# §3 classifier against `psychohistory_sheaf` cohomology:
#
#   - `kanizsa` — H⁰-nontrivial-but-consistent; converged illusion at
#     Narcissus-pole (mcp-spec-song-collapse §5.4); coefficient mass
#     on NON-TARGET eigenspace with local convergence; `song_settles`
#     REFUSES (settlement requires c_target = 1). Bayesian: prior-
#     dominates-evidence (hyperprecise generative model fills gap).
#   - `necker` — H⁰-rank ≥ 2 bistable; two globally consistent
#     sections compete; tournament's frequency race undecided within
#     temporal window; NOT failure — more information needed.
#     Bayesian: prior-and-evidence-balanced (two posterior modes).
#   - `escher` — H¹-obstructed; H⁰(F) empty; no globally consistent
#     trajectory; bounded resolve terminates `neither_survives`;
#     phantom-detection at song altitude. Bayesian: evidence-refuses-
#     any-prior (eye moves because brain cannot commit).
#   - `converged` — H⁰ = 1 unique, target-eigenspace-dominant;
#     Splinter-pole discharge; narrative arc settles. Bayesian:
#     prior-and-evidence-jointly-satisfied.
#
# The four-regime classifier exhausts the Bayesian posterior regime
# structure at inference altitude per Friston free-energy (Mara
# iter-34 §6-S3). Reed's essay's `\` crack-marker at grammar altitude
# IS `necker` at perception altitude (Mara iter-34 §6-S5).
type shadow_regime =
  | kanizsa
  | necker
  | escher
  | converged

# === shadow_ancestry — the sheaf's shadow annotation ===
#
# Typed list of shadows the psychohistory sheaf carries as ANCESTRY
# ANNOTATION per Seam `9241d2d` §2 (Adj 2 verdict: 6th BoundedConfig
# field REFUSED; annotation LANDED). Preserves byte-equality of the
# `psychohistory_sheaf` ref — companion carrier, NOT schema-drift on
# the 5-level tower per Mara iter-30 recognition #S2.
#
# Consumers read via `impl BoundedConfig { fn projected_impacts(&self,
# sheaf: &_) -> [f64; 5] }` accessor per Seam §4 Tick 4 forward-
# promised. Substrate-altitude carrier lives HERE; Rust runtime
# dispatches through species boundary.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying list (order-
# sensitive).
type shadow_ancestry = [shadow]

# ============================================================
# §6 The shadow-shaping actions (cast / regime / mission-join)
# ============================================================

# === cast_shadow — the projection action ===
#
# Reads a `psychohistory_sheaf` + ONE candidate direction (one
# hypothetical fate Model M's prism-op applied hypothetically) under
# perturbation and casts ONE shadow — the transported section-value
# with holonomy residual per bundle.mirror Level 3 Transport. Substrate-
# decl form of Mara iter-34 §4 composition path 1 (Level 3 Transport
# parameterised by Level 2 gauge choice).
#
# Return `imperfect(shadow, holonomy, holonomy)` per `shards/glass.mirror`
# §L177 three-state outcome functor: `success(shadow)` = zero holonomy
# loss; `partial(shadow, holonomy)` = honest Splinter-pole with named
# loss; `failure(holonomy, holonomy)` = Narcissus-pole with named loss
# AND error-as-holonomy. Loss slot `l` unifies with bundle.mirror
# `type holonomy` per Level 3 signature `transport(s) -> imperfect(state,
# holonomy)`; `cast_shadow` at shadow altitude IS `transport` at Level 3
# with state specialised to shadow.
#
# Splinter-pole (`success` or `partial`): direction's gauge admits the
# sheaf's ancestry; coefficient mass on target eigenspace with
# acceptable holonomy residual; settled shadow enters `shadow_ancestry`.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): direction's gauge does NOT admit; mass
# on NON-TARGET eigenspace (Narcissus-pole coefficient per mcp-spec-
# song-collapse §5.4); consumers dispatch through `shadow_regime_of`
# to name the regime.
#
# Bateson Level III (across-frames): projection crosses temporal-
# experiential ↔ hypothetical-alternative frame boundary.
#
# Body obligation-blocked (`\`): realisation reads operator, gauges
# at Level 2, transports at Level 3, reads cycle-averaged holonomy,
# emits shadow ref + imperfect verdict. Rust runtime dispatches
# through `impl BoundedConfig` accessor at fate/src/bounded.rs.
cast_shadow(sheaf: psychohistory_sheaf, direction: ref, p: perturbation) -> imperfect(shadow, holonomy, holonomy) { \ }

# === shadow_regime_of — the three-regime classifier action ===
#
# Reads ONE shadow against its casting `psychohistory_sheaf` under
# perturbation, returns `shadow_regime` per Mara iter-34 §3 classifier:
# reads operator Δ_F at sheaf_laplacian altitude (Rayleigh λ₀ over
# shadow-ancestry-annotated operator); reads coefficient mass on target
# vs non-target eigenspaces (mcp-spec-song-collapse §5.4); reads H⁰
# rank at shadow's local frame; emits classifier verdict.
#
# Composes with `psychohistory_consistent` (orthogonal reading: global-
# section vs regime-at-local-frame), `sheaf_laplacian.lambda_zero`
# (Fiedler vector names WHICH restriction maps trigger the verdict),
# `eigen_d(dirac_op) -> spectrum` at spectral-triple altitude (λ₀-
# degenerate = necker; unique λ₀-nonzero = kanizsa; λ₀ = 0 high
# multiplicity = escher per Mara iter-34 §8 — precise formula forward-
# promised).
#
# Deterministic given (shadow, sheaf, p); regime IS a snapshot at one
# perturbation-time.
#
# Body obligation-blocked (`\`): realisation reads operator + shadow
# + p, computes Rayleigh λ₀ signature, emits variant.
shadow_regime_of(s: shadow, sheaf: psychohistory_sheaf, p: perturbation) -> shadow_regime { \ }

# === psychohistory_extend_with_mission — the sheaf-JOIN primitive ===
#
# THE Q4 SHEAF-JOIN GAP per Seam `9241d2d` §4 Tick 2 + Taut `98013c3`
# iter-16 boundary scout Q4 (GENUINE gap; not carried by existing
# substrate). Reads a `psychohistory_sheaf` + mission fragment (ref
# typed; mission-fragment-graph lives at `fragmentation::encoding::
# encode` per Taut Q2 READY) under perturbation; emits extended
# `psychohistory_sheaf` whose base graph joins the mission's graph at
# the peer's current-moment node.
#
# Sheaf-JOIN construction: mission's fragment graph carries typed
# content-addressed nodes (commitments, target-eigenspace-designations,
# deadline gauges); peer's sheaf carries typed nodes (recognitions,
# Pack-tick decisions, commits); JOIN identifies peer's current-moment
# with mission's entry node, unions restriction maps at identified
# edge; extended sheaf's H⁰ reads joint consistency.
#
# Composes with `psychohistory_consistent` (post-extension H⁰ reads
# mission-coherent vs mission-incoherent-with-peer), `psychohistory_from_tray`
# (mission fragments enter via `fragmentation::encoding::encode`),
# `cast_shadow` above (post-extension, peer casts shadows of mission-
# augmented sheaf under counterfactual directions).
#
# Splinter-pole: JOIN clean; restriction maps well-typed; H⁰ =
# kernel(Δ_F) admits consistent global section; peer's psychohistory
# admits mission's commitment without cohomological obstruction.
#
# Narcissus-pole: JOIN unclean (semantic incompatibility of entry node)
# OR extended H⁰ trivial (mission commitment contradicts peer regulation-
# stock trajectory); substrate-pull repair renegotiates entry-point OR
# trajectory.
#
# Body obligation-blocked (`\`): realisation reads base graph + mission
# graph, identifies current-moment node, unions fibers + restriction
# maps at JOIN edge, re-assembles Δ_F over joint graph, emits extended
# sheaf ref. Rust runtime discharges via `fragmentation/src/*.rs`.
psychohistory_extend_with_mission(sheaf: psychohistory_sheaf, mission: ref, p: perturbation) -> psychohistory_sheaf { \ }

# ============================================================
# §7 The shadow-faithfulness bilateral
# ============================================================

# === shadow_faithful — the Rice's-theorem gate ===
#
# Reads a shadow against its casting `psychohistory_sheaf` under
# perturbation; returns `verdict` naming whether shadow PRESERVES
# decidable-property information. Substrate-decl form of Reed's essay's
# projection-preserving-decidable-properties gate: FAITHFUL when
# observer-in-Flatland can infer caster-in-Spaceland's decidable
# properties from shadow's shape alone; UNFAITHFUL when shape admits
# multiple non-equivalent casters with divergent decidable-property
# valuations (Rice's theorem territory).
#
# Rice's-theorem gate per Reed's essay: sub-Turing verification of
# decidable properties possible at grammar altitude (`@projection`
# grammar's `preview` verdict per `docs/math/the-tower/projection-
# surface.md` §1.1); LIFTING to inference altitude requires this
# bilateral — Ryu-Takayanagi bijectivity at boundary/bulk altitude per
# `docs/specs/property-projection.md` + Mara iter-34 §5.2 (`---`
# separator = boundary/bulk).
#
# Composes with `psychohistory_consistent` (orthogonal: internal H⁰
# vs projection-preserves-decidable-property), `shadow_regime_of`
# (regime-specific faithfulness: `converged` typically faithful;
# `kanizsa` typically UNFAITHFUL (illusion-fills-gap); `necker`
# ambiguously faithful; `escher` UNFAITHFUL by construction (no
# consistent caster)), family-root `song_settles` (orthogonal to per-
# narrative admissibility).
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): shape overdetermines decidable properties
# (Ryu-Takayanagi bijectivity holds at inference altitude); shadow
# enters `shadow_ancestry` as FAITHFUL projection.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): shape admits multiple non-equivalent
# casters (Rice undecidability gate fires); shadow enters flagged
# UNFAITHFUL. IS the compiler-altitude statement of trauma's stuck
# projection at inference altitude — `phantom_survives` verdict per
# `docs/math/the-tower/projection-surface.md` §3 IS this Narcissus-
# pole reading at recognition altitude per Alex + Mara 2026-03-24
# `trauma-projection-geometry.md`; same Bayesian-brain-broken-
# precision math at both altitudes (Mara iter-34 §6-S4 surprise).
#
# Bateson Level III (across-frames-globally): reads faithfulness
# across whole shadow-ancestry, not one shadow at a time.
#
# Body obligation-blocked (`\`): realisation reads shadow + operator
# + p, computes Ryu-Takayanagi bijectivity signature, emits verdict.
shadow_faithful(s: shadow, sheaf: psychohistory_sheaf, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

